==Sanskrit==
{{wp|lang=sa|भारतम्}}

===Alternative scripts===
{{sa-alt}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sa|inc-pro|*bhā́ratas}}, ultimately from {{der|sa|ine-pro|*bʰer-||to carry}}. Synchronically analysable as the {{vrd|sa|भरत|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{sa-IPA|a=1}}

===Adjective===
{{sa-adj|tr=bhā́rata}}

# descended from {{m|sa|भरत}} or the [[Bhāratas]] (applied to [[Agni]] either "sprung from the priests called Bharatas" or "bearer of the [[oblation]]")
# belonging or relating to the Bharatas
## (with {{m|sa|युद्ध|tr=yuddhá}}, {{m|sa|संग्राम}}, {{m|sa|समर|tr=samará}}, {{m|sa|समिति}}) the war or battle of the bharatas
## (with or scil. {{m|sa|आख्यान}} with {{m|sa|इतिहास}} and {{m|sa|कथा}}) the story of the Bharatas, the history or narrative of their war
## (with or scil. {{m|sa|मण्डल|tr=máṇḍala}} or {{m|sa|वर्ष|tr=varṣá}}) "king Bharatas's realm" i.e. [[India]]
# inhabiting {{m|sa|भरतवर्ष|tr=bharata-varṣa}} i.e. [[India]]; [[Indic]]

====Declension====
{{sa-decl-adj|भार|त|bhāra|t|a|ī|a}}

===Noun===
{{sa-noun|tr=bhā́rata|g=m}}

# a [[descendant]] of [[Bharata]] (also in pl. for [[Bharatās]])
# (with {{m|sa|अश्वमेध|tr=aśva-medhá}}), name of the author of Rigveda V, 27
# (with {{m|sa|देववात|tr=deva-vāta}} and {{m|sa|देवश्रवस्|tr=deva-śravas}}), name of the authors of Rigveda III, 23
# [[fire]]
# an [[actor]] (compare {{m|sa|भरत}})
# name of the sun shining on the south of {{m|sa|मेरु}}

====Declension====
{{sa-decl-noun-m|bhā́rata}}

===Noun===
{{sa-noun|tr=bhā́rata|g=n}}

# the [[land]] of Bharatas i.e. [[India]] (compare above)
# the story of the Bharatas and their wars (sometimes identified with the {{m|sa|महाभारत|tr=mahā-bhārata}}, and sometimes distinguished from it)
# (with {{m|sa|सरस्|tr=sáras}}) name of a lake

====Declension====
{{sa-decl-noun-n|bhā́rata}}

